WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.150
This is a demonstration of an AI
assistant

00:03.150 --> 00:06.300
using Delegate to complete a tax
relief claim

00:06.300 --> 00:09.450
on someone's behalf. Everything shown
here, including the

00:09.450 --> 00:12.600
account and tax details, is synthetic.
This is

00:12.600 --> 00:14.568
not a live HMRC service.

00:32.000 --> 00:34.647
The request is simple: check and claim
any

00:34.647 --> 00:37.293
working from home relief available.
The assistant says

00:37.293 --> 00:39.940
it will follow the site's Delegate
journey and

00:39.940 --> 00:42.587
pause where the person's identity or
permission is

00:42.587 --> 00:45.233
needed. The service itself makes clear
this is

00:45.233 --> 00:45.895
a prototype.

01:00.000 --> 01:03.215
On the Act for someone page, the
assistant

01:03.215 --> 01:06.430
identifies itself as ChatGPT and
selects only two

01:06.430 --> 01:09.645
permissions: viewing the tax code and
claiming working

01:09.645 --> 01:12.860
from home relief. Other powers, such
as changing

01:12.860 --> 01:16.075
employment or refund details, are left
unchecked. The

01:16.075 --> 01:18.486
person gets a code to continue.

01:32.000 --> 01:34.790
The user signs into their GOV.UK
account and

01:34.790 --> 01:37.581
completes the approval step on their
phone. This

01:37.581 --> 01:40.371
is where the person authenticates and
decides whether

01:40.371 --> 01:43.162
to grant the requested access. The
assistant does

01:43.162 --> 01:45.952
not need the person's password or a
copied

01:45.952 --> 01:46.301
session.

02:06.000 --> 02:09.125
After approval, the account lists
ChatGPT as authorised

02:09.125 --> 02:12.250
for HMRC. The permission card shows
the exact

02:12.250 --> 02:15.376
scope and offers a way to remove
access.

02:15.376 --> 02:18.501
The HMRC demo then displays the
synthetic tax

02:18.501 --> 02:21.626
account and the working from home
claim option.

02:40.000 --> 02:42.487
Before submitting, the assistant
checks the eligibility

02:42.487 --> 02:45.330
question with the user: they had to
work

02:45.330 --> 02:48.173
from home and were not reimbursed. The
answer

02:48.173 --> 02:51.015
is recorded in the prototype, and the
assistant

02:51.015 --> 02:53.858
reviews the claim details against what
the user

02:53.858 --> 02:54.213
confirmed.

03:14.000 --> 03:17.058
The service accepts the claim and
displays a

03:17.058 --> 03:20.116
receipt. The assistant reports the
outcome and reminds

03:20.116 --> 03:23.174
us this is a demonstration. The
important pattern

03:23.174 --> 03:26.232
is visible: the assistant can do the
routine

03:26.232 --> 03:29.290
steps, while identity, consent, and
the claim's factual

03:29.290 --> 03:31.201
confirmation stay with the person.

03:46.000 --> 03:48.758
The user can also see who is
authorised

03:48.758 --> 03:51.516
and revoke access. Delegate gives an
agent a

03:51.516 --> 03:54.274
clear, limited route into a government
service, with

03:54.274 --> 03:57.031
the service recording the action.
Here, the whole

03:57.031 --> 03:59.789
journey uses synthetic data and does
not make

03:59.789 --> 04:00.824
a real claim.
